    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i've seen a lot of people talk about the socioeconomic stuff, but i've also seen some arguments online suggesting that there might be more fundamental or even biological reasons for these differences, like natural variations in cognitive traits or even just different cultural values regarding academic rigor. from a purely data-driven perspective, how much do experts actually weigh those kinds of internal/innate factors versus the external systemic ones?",
